Chef has N friends. Chef promised to gift a pair of shoes (consisting of one left shoe and one right shoe) to each of his friends.
Chef already has M left shoes. He needs to buy the remaining shoes from the marketplace.
Determine the minimum number of extra shoes Chef must buy so that he can gift exactly one pair of shoes to each of his N friends.

Input Format
The first line contains an integer T, the number of test cases.
Each test case consists of a single line containing two integers:
N — number of Chef’s friends
M — number of left shoes Chef already has

Output Format
For each test case, output a single integer representing the minimum number of extra shoes Chef needs to buy.


#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int main() {
	// your code goes here
	int T;
	cin>>T;
	while(T--){
	int N,M;
	cin>>N>>M;
	if(M>N){
	    cout<<N<<endl;
	}
	else{
	    int left = N*2-M;
	    cout<<left<<endl;
	    
	}
	
}
}
